{"name":"Good Graces","hex":"#f3f0d6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"good graces","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Favorable regard; personal approval; kindly treatment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good_graces"}],"entries":[{"title":"Good Graces","blocks":[{"text":"\"Good Graces\" is a song by American singer Sabrina Carpenter from her sixth studio album, Short n' Sweet (2024). The song became available as the album's third track on August 23, 2024, when it was released by Island Records. A pop and R&B song with Miami bass and UK garage influences and hip-hop rhythms, Carpenter wrote it with songwriters Julia Michaels and Amy Allen and its producers, John Ryan and Julian Bunetta."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_Graces","wikidata":"Q130213617"},{"title":"Good","blocks":[{"text":"In most contexts, the concept of good denotes the conduct that should be preferred when posed with a choice between possible actions. Good is generally considered to be the opposite of evil. The meaning and etymology of the term and its associated translations among ancient and contemporary languages show substantial variation in its inflection and meaning, depending on circumstances of place and history, or of philosophical or religious context."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good","wikidata":"Q15290"},{"title":"Charites","blocks":[{"text":"The Charites are goddesses of Greek mythology who personify beauty and grace. According to Hesiod, their names were Aglaia, Euphrosyne, and Thalia and were the daughters of Zeus and Eurynome, the daughter of Oceanus. However, their names, number and parentage varied across accounts. They have little independent mythology, and are usually described as attending various gods and goddesses, particularly Aphrodite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/The_Three_Graces%2C_from_Pompeii_%28fresco%29.jpg/330px-The_Three_Graces%2C_from_Pompeii_%28fresco%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charites","wikidata":"Q184353"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Primavera2025_%28143_of_182%29_%2854575722680%29.jpg/500px-Primavera2025_%28143_of_182%29_%2854575722680%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Primavera2025_%28143_of_182%29_%2854575722680%29.jpg/1280px-Primavera2025_%28143_of_182%29_%2854575722680%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Primavera2025_%28143_of_182%29_%2854575722680%29.jpg/500px-Primavera2025_%28143_of_182%29_%2854575722680%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carpenter performing \"Good Graces\" at Primavera Sound 2025","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrimavera2025_(143_of_182)_(54575722680).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Ariana_Grande_%2832426961944%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Ariana_Grande_%2832426961944%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Ariana_Grande_%2832426961944%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Ariana_Grande_%2832426961944%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Ariana_Grande_%2832426961944%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Ariana_Grande_%2832426961944%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Good Graces\" was compared to the works of Ariana Grande (pictured).[22]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAriana_Grande_(32426961944)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Lenz_Entwurf_zu_einem_Engel.jpg/250px-Lenz_Entwurf_zu_einem_Engel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/08/Lenz_Entwurf_zu_einem_Engel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Lenz_Entwurf_zu_einem_Engel.jpg/250px-Lenz_Entwurf_zu_einem_Engel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In many Abrahamic religions,  angels are considered to be good beings and are contrasted with demons, who are their evil counterparts.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALenz_Entwurf_zu_einem_Engel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Socrates_Pio-Clementino_Inv314.jpg/500px-Socrates_Pio-Clementino_Inv314.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Socrates_Pio-Clementino_Inv314.jpg/1280px-Socrates_Pio-Clementino_Inv314.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Socrates_Pio-Clementino_Inv314.jpg/500px-Socrates_Pio-Clementino_Inv314.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bust of Socrates in the Vatican Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASocrates_Pio-Clementino_Inv314.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Saint_Joseph%27s_Catholic_Church_%28Central_City%2C_Kentucky%29_-_stained_glass%2C_St._Thomas_Aquinas%2C_detail.jpg/500px-Saint_Joseph%27s_Catholic_Church_%28Central_City%2C_Kentucky%29_-_stained_glass%2C_St._Thomas_Aquinas%2C_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Saint_Joseph%27s_Catholic